    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryce Harper** (74.59) and **Lawrence Butler** (72.31) headline our lineup as the premier starts, both benefiting from an excellent matchup against Junk. The high scores for this pair are driven by a combination of favorable park factors and the +12% SP skill advantage afforded by the opponent's projected efficiency. While **Justin Crawford** and **Luis Arraez** also draw that same favorable matchup, **Bryce Harper** remains the most reliable anchor given his elite xwOBA of .389. We are also leaning into **Masyn Winn** (60.12); while he is buried in the order at #7, his score is bolstered by a +17% SP skill advantage and a \"Slow SP Delivery\" tag that significantly raises his stolen base probability\u2014a critical lever given our scarcity-focused strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Gavin Sheets**, who posted a 40.99 score against McLean. While **Gavin Sheets** offered a solid platoon edge, he was ultimately edged out by the superior raw efficiency of the lower-order hitters who benefit from more favorable matchup dynamics against weaker arms. We are keeping a close eye on **Braden Montgomery** (44.51), as his matchup against Imanaga is our most precarious; while the park factor provides a slight cushion, Imanaga\u2019s skill level demands we remain cautious regarding his game cap contribution. With **Will Smith** still on the IL and **Cal Raleigh** and **Daulton Varsho** idle due to off-days, our bench depth is intentionally thin to preserve our remaining cap space for high-leverage spots later in the week.",
